HST Office: in the C locale the gtk3 dialogs and panels show their .ui texts in the UI language, not English (vcl).

GtkBuilder translates the .ui texts through gettext. glibc's gettext ignores LANGUAGE (which the office sets to its
UI language) when the LC_MESSAGES locale is C or POSIX, C.UTF-8 included. An office started in such a locale with
the Vietnamese UI (gtk3) showed the strings from the code in Vietnamese and every .ui text in English: the File
panel's items, the Print page's labels (Printer, Range and Copies, Page Setup, More Options, Whole Page), dialogs.
gen and Windows (VclBuilder) translate with LibreOffice's own catalogs and were not affected. In that case
load_ui_file now gives GtkBuilder the file with its translatable texts translated by those catalogs for the UI
language (vcl::hst::TranslateUiFileForGtkBuilder: the interface's domain, each text's context, as VclBuilder) and
the translatable flags removed. Other locales, and an English UI, load the file as before.

The domain goes to Translate::Create as a NUL-terminated copy: a view into the file made boost::locale read
the rest of the .ui as the domain name and its encoding, so the first .ui of a catalog not used before (cui: Tip
of the Day, Format > Paragraph) left that catalog without texts and throwing for non-ASCII texts (abort).

Test: tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-repeat.py under LANG=C.UTF-8 with the Vietnamese UI (each opening: the
panel is in Vietnamese).
